using System;

public class CharCounter
{
    public static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Enter a string:");
        string inputString = Console.ReadLine();

        Console.WriteLine("Enter a character to count:");
        char targetChar = Console.ReadKey().KeyChar;
        Console.WriteLine(); // Move to the next line after reading the character

        int count = 0;
        foreach (char c in inputString)
        {
            if (c == targetChar)
            {
                count++;
            }
        }

        Console.WriteLine($"The character '{targetChar}' appears {count} times in the string.");
    }
}
```

This C# program prompts the user for a string and a character. It then iterates through the string, comparing each character to the target character.  If a match is found, a counter is incremented. Finally, the program displays the total count of the character's occurrences within the input string.  The `Console.ReadKey().KeyChar` method efficiently captures a single character input without requiring the user to press Enter.  The program utilizes a `foreach` loop for concise string traversal.
